                <pb facs="0526" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/205c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-23T20:00:00-05:00">December 23, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>373. Department has been informed from an official source of indiscreet
                    utterances attributed to a Japanese employee of Japanese Navy to the effect that
                    the sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> was deliberately planned,
                    by whom not stated, to bring to light the attitude of the United States as
                    bearing on further Japanese action; that a Japanese Navy ace, Captain Minami,
                    was in charge of the bombing; that Minami is stationed at Sasebo and after the
                    sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> returned there; and that there
                    have been planned further similar acts against Great Britain and the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
